  "scope": "An actual fundamental SU(2) Wilson obstruction for the current affine a^-4 plaquette hierarchy. Certified excess moments and exact Haar inversion/rotation give a radial conditional covariance floor. On the actual good-staple event, every nonnegative source weight has radial projection at least half its incident weight sum; the proved actual-law entropy bound yields annealed variance at least W_link^2/(384 beta^2). Exact eight-color independent-block disintegration bounds the sum of these actual one-link variances by 8 times the full original-law source variance, with arbitrary deterministic identity counterterms. A concrete real nonnegative compact smooth Schwartz test has integral 1. Actual floor/residue sampling and finite incidence counting give at most (9/a)^4 relevant plaquettes independently of the torus period, so the rescaled ordinary second moment is at least a^-4/(768*9^4 beta^2). It diverges on every positive vanishing mesh with beta->infinity and an eventual positive logarithmic upper bound, for any even lattice periods>1 and any identity counterterms. Exact ordinary tensor-moment identities bind this to the unmodified affine Wilson hierarchy. This does not prove or disprove the separate reflected bracket endpoint signs, and does not exclude contact-renormalized, differently normalized, or different observable continuum theories.",
  "actual_noise_chain": {
    "conditional": "Given an actual exterior, kappa=2 beta ||A||, Var[kappa(1-q_parallel)]>=3/4 for kappa>=50. Haar inversion removes mixed radial/transverse terms in the variance lower estimate.",
    "weighted_projection": "For six unit staples and ||A||>=11/2, each <A/||A||,v_p>>=1/2; arbitrary nonnegative actual source weights therefore have radial projection at least W_link/2.",
    "annealed": "Conditional variance>=W_link^2/(192 beta^2); actual bad-event probability<=36 energyEnvelope(beta), so energyEnvelope<=1/72 gives annealed floor W_link^2/(384 beta^2). Thresholds hold eventually as beta->infinity, uniformly in lattice period.",
    "aggregation": "Eight actual independent color blocks yield sum_link E Var_link<=8 Var(fullsource). Every actual source plaquette is incident to four links; occupied-link Cauchy retains only compact source support size.",
    "fixed_test": "A single normalized nonnegative smooth bump of radius2 and integral 1, pulled back to Configuration1 and tensored with itself for the ordinary two-point hierarchy.",
    "support_count": "Integer floor cells meeting the radius2 ball lie in |z_mu|<=ceil_nat(2/a)+1. Periodic residue mapping only reduces cardinality. For0<a<=1, source plaquette support card<=(9/a)^4 independently of n; no no-alias or finite-box hypothesis.",
    "lower_bound": "E_W[(a^-4 S_f-c)^2]>=a^-4/(768*9^4 beta^2), for every real c, even n>1, beta>=5 and energyEnvelope(beta)<=1/72.",
    "divergence": "For every a_k>0->0, beta_k->infinity and eventual beta_k<=b log(1/a_k) with b>0, this lower bound tends to infinity independently of the even volume path and identity counterterm.",
    "hierarchy_dictionary": "For the normalized real test, affine trace insertion scale*(trace-center) equals minus(scale*defectSource-scale*(2-center)); its ordinary tensor-square hierarchy value is exactly the real second moment."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The current a^-4 plaquette insertion with only deterministic identity subtraction cannot satisfy common full two-point Schwartz bounds on a diverging logarithmic weak-coupling trajectory: its fixed smooth-test ordinary second moment diverges. The new obstruction is uniform in the even lattice period, not only a coincident-point statement or a special-volume counterpath.",
    "Construct a revised observable or a contact-renormalized hierarchy, including actual nonperturbative counterterm coefficients, all-order partial-diagonal compatibility, uniform bounds, and its own reflection/translation/continuum transport. The current affine proposedSequence cannot silently be replaced by such a hierarchy.",
    "Actual positive separated reflected-signal lower estimates and logarithmic bracket endpoint signs remain unproved. The ordinary variance lower bound is ultraviolet conditional noise; no separated physical signal, physical coupling identification, or mass gap follows from it.",
    "Prove a nonzero collective physical-transfer source with controlled norm and relative Dirichlet energy D(w_a)/||w_a||^2<=C*a along an independently justified physical coupling trajectory. Existing absolute energy bounds and scalar normalization do not supply this.",
    "Construct compatible infinite-volume/ultraviolet limits with complete Euclidean/Poincare covariance, physical field/domain/cyclicity/spectrum/locality properties and every required compact simple gauge group. All twelve full Clay requirements remain open; no nonzero continuum or physical mass gap is claimed."
  ],
